11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Based on the DC character Teth-Adam / Black Adam,
the film is a spin-off from Shazam!

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
(2019) and the eleventh film in the DC Extended Universe (DCEU).

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Directed by Jaume Collet-Serra from a screenplay by Adam Sztykiel, Rory Haines and Sohrab Noshirvani, the film follows Teth-Adam / Black Adam, an ancient superhuman who is released from his magic imprisonment by
a group of archeologists to free the nation of Kahndaq from the crime syndicate Intergang, whose local leader plans to obtain an ancient relic called the Crown of Sabbac to take control of it.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Aldis Hodge, Noah Centineo, Sarah Shahi, Quintessa Swindell, Marwan
Kenzari and Pierce Brosnan appear in supporting roles.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Johnson was attached to Shazam!

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
early in development and confirmed to portray the villain Black Adam in September 2014, but the
producers, at Johnson's urging, later decided to give the character his own film.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Sztykiel was hired in October 2017.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Collet-Serra joined in June 2019 with a planned release date of December
2021, but this timeline was delayed by the COVID-19 pandemic.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Additional casting took place over the next year, including four members of the Justice
Society of America, along with the script being rewritten by Haines and Noshirvani.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Principal photography took place from April to August 2021 at Trilith
Studios in Atlanta, Georgia, and also in Los Angeles.

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
Black Adam premiered in Mexico City on October 3, 2022, and was
theatrically released in the United States on October 21.

22
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
It received mixed-to-negative reviews from critics and failed to break-even at the box
office, grossing $393 million worldwide against a budget of $190–$260 million.

